A||N||3||Seanh||Best source for front 84-87 brake calipers?||||1||
Z||000000||Seanh||06-22-2001||01:00 PM||||Were is the cheapest place to get a pair of new (or rebuilt) front brake calipers for my 86 GT? I took mine off, and was going to rebuild them with new seals, but can't get the damn piston out of the bore. I tried compressed air, but it just leaks out of the hole I put it in, so that didn't work at all. Or, could someone tell me how to get the piston out? Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||ferg||06-22-2001||02:06 PM||||I don't know if this will help, I opened the bleeder screw and let air into the brake system (was planning on replacing fluid anyway) then closed the bleeder,then my dad pumped the brakes, piston came out really far- I opened the bleeder screw again and the piston shot out of the caliper. I did this on the rear caliper, so I'm not sure if it will work on the front, but it's worth a try. You probably know to put a hose on the bleeder screw to direct the fluid into a container.<P>Also, my local auto supply store (independant- not pep boys or autozone) said for $75/ea I could buy a rebuilt rear caliper. I would figure on spending around that much for the front.<P>My car is also an 86GT. you can see pics of the rear piston on my website<BR> <A HREF="http://pages.prodigy.net/fergusor" TARGET=_blank>http://pages.prodigy.net/fergusor</A> <P>go to the link that says 'my upgrade pics'<P>hope this helps.<p>[This message has been edited by ferg (edited 06-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Kevin-84SE||06-22-2001||03:14 PM||||You may want to check your local NAPA or other parts store, I got replacement calipers from NAPA, I think they were about $40 each<P>   Kevin||||reg||1
Z||000003||Seanh||06-22-2001||03:22 PM||||I'm such a dumbass! Why didn't I ever think to put the calipers back on and pump the brakes! I'll try that tonight. Thanks!||||reg||1
